LWho is yet another replacement for the regular DLG:Who (who's online)
module.

It is loosely based on Greg Bastow's rexx version.  I am trying to
purge my system of all rexx programs and this was the last to go.

LWho is provided "as is" with no guarantees.  It is FREEWARE.
I cannot be held responsible for any damage to your system
believed to be caused by LWho.  Use it at your own risk.

Setup:

  USAGE:  LWho <port> ... <port>
  
  Where <port> ... <port> is a list of ports you wish to scan.
  
    EXAMPLE:  LWho TR0 TR1 TR2 TL0 TL1 TL2


Example DLG Menu entry:

[ 1] Letter:                   W
[ 2] Executable: (path/name)   DLX:LWho TR0 TL0 TL1 TL2 TRX
[ 4] Description:              Who's Online
[ 5] Type:                     Executable
[ 6] Help File:                MAIN/W
[ 7] Lower level:              5
[ 8] Upper level:              255
[ 9] Hidden:                   NO
[10] Load type:                OVERLAY
[11] Ask user if sure:         NO
[12] Pend messages:            YES
[13] Cli mode:                 NO
[14] Pause on completion:      NO
[15] Log value:                None
[16] Activity string:          Main Menu - Snooping On Other Users...
[17] Priority:                 DEFAULT

Notes:

   LWho may be called from offline, given the appropriate list of ports.
   
   When called from online, it adheres to the users ANSI color/mono settings
   and is even aware of how tall their screen is (for those of you with more
   than 24 or so ports -- is that anyone?) ...
   
   The only checking I do for port names is whether or not you have supplied
   a three character designation.  Feel free to list ports more than once
   if for any reason you'd like to see multiple entries for that port ;)

